Milan's piazza del duomo normally  bustling now virtually at a standstill  the corona virus outbreak in northern  Italy's Lombardy region means even the  site's historic Duomo Cathedral is  closed to visitors and many here aren't  happy I hope next week they managed to  solve the problem because the  restaurants are empty the cafes are  empty the trams and trains are empty I  don't know how long we can cope with the  situation since the first coronavirus  case was detected in Italy the stock  exchange has plunged 8% making many  worry about how exactly the fragile  economy will cope it's not just tourists  who are missing from this famous square  it's also residents many of whom now  find themselves working from home like  Mara Monti an academic coordinator at a  university in Milan who's trying to keep  things calm for her family so they can  all adapt to the situation the concern  is there I receive messages from all  over the word from my students and over  the world a concern that they are  concerned about me about my situation by  the university my family Mata wants to  make sure her son and daughter take the  necessary precautions by the sound of it  her advice has already made an impact  I always bring my sunny ties in in gel  with me like yesterday when I was having  ice cream with my girlfriends and I made  them all wash their hands at night  Milan looks and feels even emptier  tables with no one to sit around them  waiting staff with no one to serve  before we have much customer boots now  everywhere is dried off even industries  they made sure the sky is dark but so is  the mood yes the trams still run even  though it seems more and more uncertain  where things are heading Mohammed  Abdullah Al Jazeera Milan
 

